# Rewritten to remove three problems: the C++ and logging blocks were duplicated
# verbatim; the trailing `!docs/`, `!*.png`, `!*.pdf` negations were no-ops,
# because nothing above them excluded those paths and a negation cannot re-include
# a file whose parent directory is excluded; and `*.csv` silently covered the run
# logs the README presents as evidence. Run outputs now live under output/ (see
# sdhcal/paths.py), which is excluded wholesale, while the curated logs that are
# already tracked stay tracked - .gitignore does not affect tracked files.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
*.env

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and operating systems
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.bak

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# C++ / ROOT build products
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.o
*.so
*.a
*.d
*.dll
*.dylib
*.exe
*.pcm
*_C.so
*_C_ACLiC_dict*
build/
cmake-build-*/
analysis/1_shower_features/extract
analysis/1_shower_features/extract_parallel
analysis/archive/build/
analysis/archive/cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Detector data and generated tables
#
# None of these are versioned: they are too large and depend on the simulation
# and digitisation environment. See docs/data_pipeline.md for how to produce
# them, and set SDHCAL_DATA_DIR to point at them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.root
*.slcio
*.csv
*.tsv
*.npz
*.npy
data/
datasets/
# The sharded parameter lots of the two-class study: inputs, not artifacts, and
# several GB of them. Their *.root files are already covered above; naming the
# directories keeps a stray log or manifest out too.
new_data/
new_data_params/
new_data_params_v2/
local_data/

# The chi2 calibration is small, textual and the single source of truth shared
# by the C++ and Python sides, so it is versioned.
!calibration/chi2_coefficients.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.joblib
*.pkl
*.h5
*.onnx
models/
checkpoints/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run outputs
#
# Everything a pipeline writes - plots, per-run JSON, arrays, tables - goes
# under output/ by default (SDHCAL_OUT_DIR). Promote a figure by copying it into
# results/ and adding it explicitly.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
output/
runs/
wandb/
*.log
nohup.out
core
core.*
*.tmp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LaTeX build products
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.aux
*.bbl
*.bcf
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.lof
*.lot
*.out
*.run.xml
*.synctex.gz
*.toc
*.nav
*.snm
*.vrb
report/build/

# Historical files moved out of the active analysis tree remain versioned so a
# commit records renames rather than silent deletions. Rebuildable binaries and
# bytecode stay ignored through the explicit archive/build and archive/cache
# rules above.
!analysis/archive/
!analysis/archive/README.md
!analysis/archive/code/
!analysis/archive/code/**
!analysis/archive/results/
!analysis/archive/results/**
